[936.005263, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.005284, "o", "> "]
[936.005317, "o", "§2. Definitions and special rules\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.005339, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.00536, "o", "> "]
[936.005397, "o", "(b) Definition of head of household\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.005418, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.00544, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.005461, "o", "Lines 204-216:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.005481, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.005507, "o", "    (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.005535, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.005543, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.005817, "o", "    An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.005869, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.005891, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.006073, "o", "        (A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.006096, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.00613, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.006321, "o", "            (ii) any other person who is a dependent of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such person under section 151,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.006342, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.006362, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.006384, "o", "## Reasoning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.006405, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.006766, "o", "1. **Filing Status**: Alice is unmarried and maintains a household where Bob (her nephew) lived. Under §2(b)(1) (lines 204-216), Alice qualifies as \"head of household\" because she is not married, not a surviving spouse, and maintains a household where her dependent Bob lives.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.006806, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.00694, "o", "2. **Bob as Dependent**: Bob qualifies as a \"qualifying relative\" under §152(d) (lines 147-157) because:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.006962, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.007075, "o", "   - He bears a relationship to Alice as her brother's son (§152(d)(2)(E), lines 158-167)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.007097, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.007118, "o", "> "]
[936.007162, "o", "   - He has no income (§152(d)(1)(B), lines 155-156)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.007184, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.007317, "o", "   - He is not a qualifying child of any other taxpayer (Charlie had a different principal place of abode)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.007337, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.007362, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.007658, "o", "3. **Standard Deduction**: For 2019 (taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017), under §151(c)(2) and §151(c)(7) (lines 393-397 and 426-431), the basic standard deduction for a head of household is $18,000 (substituted for $4,400).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.007701, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.007724, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.007964, "o", "4. **Exemptions**: Under §151(b) and §151(c) (lines 62-64), Alice gets an exemption for herself plus an exemption for each dependent. Under §151(d)(1) (lines 66-72), the exemption amount is $2,000. Alice gets:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.007983, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.008002, "o", "> "]
[936.008021, "o", "   - $2,000 for herself\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.008038, "o", "> "]
[936.00807, "o", "   - $2,000 for Bob as dependent\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008091, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.008126, "o", "   - Total exemptions: $4,000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008148, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.008169, "o", "> "]
[936.008204, "o", "5. **Taxable Income Calculation**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008225, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.008271, "o", "   - Gross income: $34,510 (case fact)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008279, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.008302, "o", "> "]
[936.008383, "o", "   - Standard deduction: $18,000 (§151(c)(2)(B) modified by §151(c)(7))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008402, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.008459, "o", "   - Exemptions: $4,000 (§151(d)(1) × 2)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008477, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.008561, "o", "   - Taxable income = $34,510 - $18,000 - $4,000 = $12,510\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008576, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.008593, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.008614, "o", "> "]
[936.008775, "o", "6. **Tax Calculation**: Under §1(b)(i) (line 23), for head of household with taxable income not over $29,600, tax is 15% of taxable income.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008812, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[936.008843, "o", "   - Tax = 15% × $12,510 = $1,876.50\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[936.008864, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[936.008886, "o", "> "]
[936.00891, "o", "   - Rounded to whole number: $1,877\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
