[1444.452676, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> Lines 120-143:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     The term \"qualifying child\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (B) who has the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (C) who meets the age requirements of paragraph (3), and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (E) who has not filed a joint return (other than only for a claim of refund) with the individual's spouse for the taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (d) Qualifying relative\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Lines 144-157:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.452739, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>     (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     The term \"qualifying relative\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (B) who has no income for the calendar year in which such taxable year begins, and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (D) who is not a qualifying child of such taxpayer or of any other taxpayer for any taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which such taxable year begins.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     (2) Relationship\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     Lines 158-167:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r dependent\r\n   - Total exemptions: $4,000\r\n\r\n5. **Taxable Income Calculation**:\r\n   - Gross income: $34,510 (case fact)\r\n   - Standard deduction: $18,000 (§151(c)(2)(B) modified by §151(c)(7))\r\n   - Exemptions: $4,000 (§151("]
[1444.452752, "o", "d)(1) × 2)\r\n   - Taxable income = $34,510 - $18,000 - $4,000 = $12,510\r\n\r\n6. **Tax Calculation**: Under §1(b)(i) (line 23), for head of household with taxable income not over $29,600, tax is 15% of taxable income.\r\n   - Tax = 15% × $12,510 = $1,876.50\r\n   - Rounded to whole number: $1,877\r\n\r\n## Answer\r\nAnswer: 1877\r\nEOF\r\n\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453018, "o", "    For purposes of paragraph (1)(A), an individual bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in this paragraph if the individual is any of the following with respect to the taxpayer:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.45304, "o", "        (E) A son or daughter of a brother or sister of the taxpayer.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
