[1444.453053, "o", "> "]
[1444.453273, "o", "§151. Standard deduction\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Lines 393-397:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453318, "o", "        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453372, "o", "        (C) $3,000 in any other case.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.453382, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453388, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.453399, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453506, "o", "§151(c)(7) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.453582, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453602, "o", "Lines 426-431:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453653, "o", "    (7) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.453661, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453666, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.453677, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453861, "o", "    In the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[1444.453871, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.453908, "o", "    Paragraph (2) shall be applied-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.453916, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.454021, "o", "        (i) by substituting \"$18,000\" for \"$4,400\" in subparagraph (B), and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454028, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.454033, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454047, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.454196, "o", "        (ii) by substituting \"$12,000\" for \"$3,000\" in subparagraph (C).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.454248, "o", "§2. Definitions and special rules\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454265, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.454309, "o", "(b) Definition of head of household\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454316, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.454321, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454334, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.454339, "o", "> "]
[1444.45436, "o", "Lines 204-216:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454369, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.454375, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454383, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.454405, "o", "> "]
[1444.454501, "o", "    (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454538, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.454729, "o", "    An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454752, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[1444.454773, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.454782, "o", "> "]
[1444.454992, "o", "        (A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.454999, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.455009, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.45502, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.455025, "o", "> "]
[1444.455244, "o", "            (ii) any other person who is a dependent of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such person under section 151,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.455251, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.455263, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.455269, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.455275, "o", "> "]
[1444.455295, "o", "## Reasoning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.455305, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.45531, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.455322, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.455329, "o", "> "]
[1444.455699, "o", "1. **Filing Status**: Alice is unmarried and maintains a household where Bob (her nephew) lived. Under §2(b)(1) (lines 204-216), Alice qualifies as \"head of household\" because she is not married, not a surviving spouse, and maintains a household where her dependent Bob lives.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.45571, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.455716, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.455726, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.455887, "o", "2. **Bob as Dependent**: Bob qualifies as a \"qualifying relative\" under §152(d) (lines 144-157) because:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.455948, "o", "> "]
[1444.456011, "o", "   - He bears a relationship to Alice as her brother's son (§152(d)(2)(E), lines 158-167)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.456026, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.456089, "o", "   - He has no income (§152(d)(1)(B), line 155)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.456105, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.456567, "o", "   - He is not a qualifying child of any taxpayer: Bob lived at Alice's place, not Charlie's place. Under §152(c)(1)(B) (line 136), a qualifying child must have \"the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year.\" Since Charlie had a different principal place of abode, Bob is NOT Charlie's qualifying child.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.456603, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.456907, "o", "3. **Standard Deduction**: For 2019 (taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017), under §151(c)(2) and §151(c)(7) (lines 393-397 and 426-431), the basic standard deduction for a head of household is $18,000 (substituted for $4,400).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.456925, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.456939, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.457217, "o", "4. **Exemptions**: Under §151(b) and §151(c) (lines 62-64), Alice gets an exemption for herself plus an exemption for each dependent. Under §151(d)(1) (lines 66-72), the exemption amount is $2,000. Alice gets:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457231, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.457273, "o", "   - $2,000 for herself\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457287, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.457333, "o", "   - $2,000 for Bob as dependent\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457346, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.457388, "o", "   - Total exemptions: $4,000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457405, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.45742, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.457472, "o", "5. **Taxable Income Calculation**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457486, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.45754, "o", "   - Gross income: $34,510 (case fact)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457557, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.457657, "o", "   - Standard deduction: $18,000 (§151(c)(2)(B) modified by §151(c)(7))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.45767, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.457729, "o", "   - Exemptions: $4,000 (§151(d)(1) × 2)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457743, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.457821, "o", "   - Taxable income = $34,510 - $18,000 - $4,000 = $12,510\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457834, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.457847, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.45786, "o", "> "]
[1444.458036, "o", "6. **Tax Calculation**: Under §1(b)(i) (line 23), for head of household with taxable income not over $29,600, tax is 15% of taxable income.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.458051, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.458105, "o", "   - Tax = 15% × $12,510 = $1,876.50\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.458118, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.458172, "o", "   - Rounded to whole number: $1,877\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.458187, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.458202, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.458222, "o", "## Answer\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.458238, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.458257, "o", "Answer: 1877\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.45827, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1444.458287, "o", "EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1444.46091, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1444.460923, "o", "root@e734b4c2d1a5:/app# "]
[1453.510704, "i", "cat /app/output/answer.txt\n"]
[1453.510902, "o", "cat /app/output/answer.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1453.511609, "o", "## Statute\r\n\r\n§1. Tax imposed\r\n\r\n(b) Heads of households\r\n\r\nLines 20-23:\r\n\r\n    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $29,600;\r\n\r\n§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions\r\n\r\n(c) Additional exemption for dependents\r\n\r\nLines 62-64:\r\n\r\n    An exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year.\r\n\r\n(d) Exemption amount\r\n\r\nLines 66-72:\r\n\r\n    (1) In general\r\n\r\n    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"exemption amount\" means $2,000.\r\n\r\n§152. Dependent defined\r\n\r\n(c) Qualifying child\r\n\r\nLines 120-143:\r\n\r\n    (1) In general\r\n\r\n    The term \"qualifying child\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\r\n\r\n        (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\r\n\r\n        (B) who has the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year,\r\n\r\n        (C) who meets the age requirements "]
[1453.511677, "o", "of paragraph (3), and\r\n\r\n        (E) who has not filed a joint return (other than only for a claim of refund) with the individual's spouse for the taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins.\r\n\r\n(d) Qualifying relative\r\n\r\nLines 144-157:\r\n\r\n    (1) In general\r\n\r\n    The term \"qualifying relative\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\r\n\r\n        (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\r\n\r\n        (B) who has no income for the calendar year in which such taxable year begins, and\r\n\r\n        (D) who is not a qualifying child of such taxpayer or of any other taxpayer for any taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which such taxable year begins.\r\n\r\n    (2) Relationship\r\n\r\n    Lines 158-167:\r\n\r\n    For purposes of paragraph (1)(A), an individual bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in this paragraph if the individual is any of the following with respect to the taxpayer:\r\n\r\n        (E) "]
[1453.511697, "o", "A son or daughter of a brother or sister of the taxpayer.\r\n\r\n§151. Standard deduction\r\n\r\nLines 393-397:\r\n\r\n        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\r\n\r\n        (C) $3,000 in any other case.\r\n\r\n§151(c)(7) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025\r\n\r\nLines 426-431:\r\n\r\n    (7) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025\r\n\r\n    In the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026-\r\n\r\n    Paragraph (2) shall be applied-\r\n\r\n        (i) by substituting \"$18,000\" for \"$4,400\" in subparagraph (B), and\r\n\r\n        (ii) by substituting \"$12,000\" for \"$3,000\" in subparagraph (C).\r\n\r\n§2. Definitions and special rules\r\n\r\n(b) Definition of head of household\r\n\r\nLines 204-216:\r\n\r\n    (1) In general\r\n\r\n    An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\r\n\r\n        (A) mai"]
[1453.511705, "o", "ntains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\r\n\r\n            (ii) any other person who is a dependent of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such person under section 151,\r\n\r\n## Reasoning\r\n\r\n1. **Filing Status**: Alice is unmarried and maintains a household where Bob (her nephew) lived. Under §2(b)(1) (lines 204-216), Alice qualifies as \"head of household\" because she is not married, not a surviving spouse, and maintains a household where her dependent Bob lives.\r\n\r\n2. **Bob as Dependent**: Bob qualifies as a \"qualifying relative\" under §152(d) (lines 144-157) because:\r\n   - He bears a relationship to Alice as her brother's son (§152(d)(2)(E), lines 158-167)\r\n   - He has no income (§152(d)(1)(B), line 155)\r\n   - He is not a qualifying child of any taxpayer: Bob lived at Alice's place, not Charlie's place. Under §152(c)(1)(B) (line 136), a qualifying"]
[1453.511719, "o", " child must have \"the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year.\" Since Charlie had a different principal place of abode, Bob is NOT Charlie's qualifying child.\r\n\r\n3. **Standard Deduction**: For 2019 (taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017), under §151(c)(2) and §151(c)(7) (lines 393-397 and 426-431), the basic standard deduction for a head of household is $18,000 (substituted for $4,400).\r\n\r\n4. **Exemptions**: Under §151(b) and §151(c) (lines 62-64), Alice gets an exemption for herself plus an exemption for each dependent. Under §151(d)(1) (lines 66-72), the exemption amount is $2,000. Alice gets:\r\n   - $2,000 for herself\r\n   - $2,000 for Bob as dependent\r\n   - Total exemptions: $4,000\r\n\r\n5. **Taxable Income Calculation**:\r\n   - Gross income: $34,510 (case fact)\r\n   - Standard deduction: $18,000 (§151(c)(2)(B) modified by §151(c)(7))\r\n   - Exemptions: $4,000 (§151(d)(1) × 2)\r\n   - Taxable income = $34,510 - $18,000 - $4,000 = $12,510\r\n\r\n6. **Ta"]
[1453.51173, "o", "x Calculation**: Under §1(b)(i) (line 23), for head of household with taxable income not over $29,600, tax is 15% of taxable income.\r\n   - Tax = 15% × $12,510 = $1,876.50\r\n   - Rounded to whole number: $1,877\r\n\r\n## Answer\r\nAnswer: 1877\r\n"]
[1453.511987, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
